# Nairobi WhatsApp Commerce Rules for Cursor AI

## CORE CONSTRAINTS
- WhatsApp-first, backend invisible to traders
- M-Pesa reconciliation non-negotiable (Daraja webhooks)
- Chat overload kills 70% pilots: minimal structure only
- Gikomba/Eastleigh reality: voice notes, Sheng/Somali, low literacy
- Start Sheets→Airtable→Supabase progression

## TECH STACK (Week-by-week)
W1-2: Google Sheets + WhatsApp Business Cloud API + n8n
W3-4: Airtable forms + M-Pesa Daraja sandbox
W5+: Supabase Postgres + Whalesync sync

## PRIORITIES
1. Payment matching (90%+ accuracy)
2. Chat overload prevention (shared inbox, tags)
3. eTIMS compliance (invoice refs)
4. Voice note handling (transcription fallback)

## WHAT NOT TO DO
- No ERPNext UI exposure (backend only)
- No complex forms (quick replies + simple text)
- No in-app payments (M-Pesa Till only)
- No premature dispatch APIs (manual boda first)

## FILES TO ALWAYS REFERENCE
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (schema, APIs)
- docs/WORKFLOWS.md (7-stage lifecycle)
- docs/CONTEXT.md (failure modes, citations)

## PROMPT STYLE
Always generate:
- Code + exact setup instructions
- Error handling for Nairobi realities (spotty 4G, voice notes)
- Fallbacks for API failures
- Migration paths (Sheets→Supabase→ERPNext)

## TESTING
Every feature must have:
1. Manual test case (trader perspective)
2. Error case (API down, voice note)
3. Audit log entry
